WEBVTT

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:39.260
Taeguk refers to the source of everything in the Universe and the universal law in which everything continuously goes through cycles of creation and destruction.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:51.260
Pumse Taeguk symbolizes the root principle of universal philosophy and is constructed by applying the truth inherent in Taeguk's yin and yang principles.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:59.260
Taeguk Sajang stands for Jin of the 8 trigrams and symbolizes thunder which represents great strength and majesty.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:14.120
Taeguk Sajang is an intermediate stage Pumse designed for students to really start learning the basics of Taekwondo.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:25.120
Taeguk Sajang is composed of successive kicks and body twists that require the balancing of the body, which help you improve your sense of balance while moving.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:33.760
We will now take a look at the Pumse of Taeguk Sajang.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:02:43.360
Taeguk Sajang consists of five key moves, namely Sonnal Godeura Makki, Pyeon Song Geut Saewo Jireugi, Jebi Pum Anchigi, Yeopchagi, and Deung Jumeok Apchigi.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.360
These are the five key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:54.360
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:03:04.360
Sonnal Godeura Makki is a technique of defending using two hands, where the supporting hand assists when performing Sonnal Bakkan Makki.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:16.250
The hand defending the torso should be placed at the solar plexus level, while the supporting hand should be placed at the elbow level of the defending arm.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.250
The elbow of the supporting arm should be placed where it crosses the center line.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:35.710
The space between the outer wrist of the supporting arm and the torso should be about one hand blade, and the elbow should be placed naturally close to the torso.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:41.710
Be careful not to let the elbow rise due to the opening of the armpit of the supporting arm.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:51.790
Pyeon Song Geut Saewo Jireugi is a technique to pierce an opponent's pressure points using the tip of your hand.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:04:02.620
This has the effect of concentrating force in one place with high pressure, as the area of contact with an opponent is small.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:13.020
You can prevent injuries and concentrate your force by placing the index, middle, and the ring finger together in a straight line.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.020
Be careful not to let your wrist bend when performing Jireugi.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:26.690
Jeppipum Anchigi is a technique that uses Sonnal Olgul Makki and Sonnal Anchigi at the same time.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:40.100
Perform the preparatory move by placing the left hand in front of the torso and the wrist of the right hand above the shoulder.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.100
Remove unnecessary force.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:51.100
Tilt the body about 45 degrees, and then simultaneously perform Wen Sonal Olgul Makki and Oren Sonal Anchigi.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:57.800
The right hand should be placed at the neck level, with the elbows slightly bent.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:08.420
The hand that performed Anchigi should be placed at the crossing with the center line in front, and your torso should stand straight.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:16.700
Be careful not to lose balance or let your torso swerve to the right due to excessive twisting.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:25.870
Yoptagi is a technique to kick a front target sideways using a foot blade or rear sole.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:33.940
The kicking leg should be raised higher than the supporting knee above the waist.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:39.940
Bend your knee, twist your pelvis, and straighten your leg to kick.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.940
Twist the heel of the supporting leg to face the direction of the kick.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:53.020
Your shoulder, hips, and heel should form a straight line.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:59.020
Be careful not to let the heel of your supporting leg twist too early in the direction of the kick.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:06.420
All moves should be performed in one succession without interruption.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:11.420
I will show you in one quick motion by connecting them with the Yoptagi technique.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:25.180
Dung Jumeok Apchigi is a technique used to strike an opponent's face in front of you with the back of the fist.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:33.180
Your arms should cross at the solar plexus level, and the striking fist should pass under the supporting arm making an arc.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:41.970
The back of the fist should be at the philtrum level, along the center line when seen from the front.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:46.970
Be careful not to let the elbow of the striking arm point outward.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:52.220
These are the five key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:57.220
We will now look at the moves in succession, connecting each move.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:01.220
The key moves of Taeguk Sajang first part consist of

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.220
Wen Seonal Geodureo Maki

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.220
Orun Pyeon Seon Geut Saewo Jireugi

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.220
Orun Seonal Geoduro Maki

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:15.550
and Wen Pyeon Seon Geut Saewo Jireugi

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:20.550
Shift your weight to your right foot while performing Wen Seonal Geoduro Maki.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:28.550
Your left hand should prepare for Batang Seon Nullo Maki, and pull your supporting hand to your waist.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.550
Then perform Nullo Maki with your left hand while setting your right foot forward,

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:38.550
and Pyeon Seon Geut Saewo Jireugi with your right hand at the same time.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:47.530
The right elbow should lightly touch the back of your left hand when performing Jireugi.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.530
Cautions for Taeguk Sajang

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.530
First part, taking a closer look.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:08:02.130
Be careful not to let the right foot draw an arc when turning around to set your foot during Orun Apgubi.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:08.520
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.520
First part in succession while watching the video.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:23.640
The key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.640
Second part consist of

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:28.640
Orun Chaebipoom Anchigi

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:32.640
Orun Apchagi and Wen Jireugi

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.640
Wen Yeopchagi

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:40.080
Orun Yeopchagi and Orun Seonal Geoduro Maki

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:45.510
After performing Wen Yeopchagi,

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:55.030
take one step forward with the kicking foot, then connect to Orun Yeopchagi.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.030
After performing Orun Yeopchagi,

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:01.030
bend the knee and prepare for the Geoduro Maki move.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:08.700
Then set your right foot and perform Seonal Geoduro Maki at the same time.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:11.700
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:15.700
Second part in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:29.150
The key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.150
Third part consist of

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.150
Wen Pakkat Maki

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.150
Orun Apchagi

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.150
and Orun Anmaki

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:39.150
Orun Pakkat Maki

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.150
Wen Apchagi

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:43.150
and Wen Anmaki

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.150
Orun Chaebipoom Anchigi

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.150
Orun Apchagi

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.150
and Orun Dung Jumeok Apchigi

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:54.150
When turning around to set your foot with Orun Duikgubi

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:57.150
and Wen Pakkat Maki during the previous move,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.150
shift your weight to your right foot

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:03.150
and use your soul to turn and transition to Orun Duikgubi.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:07.620
Cautions for Taeguk Sajang.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:11.620
Third part, taking a closer look.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:16.620
Be careful not to twist your upper body excessively when performing Anmaki.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:21.410
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.410
Third part in succession while watching the video.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:41.870
The key moves of Taeguk Sajang.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.870
Taeguk Sajang fourth part consist of

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.870
Wen Anmaki

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.870
Orun Jirigi

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.870
Orun Anmaki

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.870
Wen Jirigi

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.870
Wen Anmaki

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.870
and Double Jirigi

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:54.870
Orun Anmaki

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:58.410
and Double Jirigi

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:01.410
When setting your foot after performing Orun Jirigi

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.410
and turning around,

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.410
shift your weight to your left foot

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:10.410
and use the soul of your left foot to spin your torso clockwise.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:14.410
Make the preparatory Anmaki move with the right arm.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:18.410
Complete Doratiki, then perform Orun Anmaki.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:25.040
Cautions for Taeguk Sajang fourth part, taking a closer look.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:31.860
Please keep in mind that it is very important to quickly connect the three consecutive moves

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.860
when going from Anmaki to Double Jirigi.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:43.660
We will now practice the moves of Taeguk Sajang fourth part in succession slowly while watching the video.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:04.780
This concludes the training for Taeguk Sajang.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.780
We will take another look at all the moves and master Pumse.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:13:03.070
We have looked at the key moves of Taeguk Sajang

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:08.070
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:13.070
Congratulations on your advancing to the intermediate level of Taekwondo.

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:18.070
We urge you to continue your efforts to improve your body's sense of balance.

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.070
We'll see you again in the Taeguk Ojang video.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.070
Thanks for watching.

